Financial Performance Data — Innovation, Science and Economic Development
Canada / Statistics Canada — Open Government Licence – Canada
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The peer-benchmark ("reasonableness") engine reads a benchmark table that is
built locally, by running `scripts/ingest_ised_benchmarks.py` against the
Financial Performance Data (FPD) release published on the Government of Canada
Open Government Portal. (Run with `--seed-only`, the same
script writes a small table of invented example figures instead, which carries
no attribution because it contains no licensed data.)

  Dataset:  Financial Performance Data (2024)
  Publisher: Innovation, Science and Economic Development Canada
  Licence:  Open Government Licence - Canada (`ca-ogl-lgo`)
            https://open.canada.ca/en/open-government-licence-canada

Verified against the portal's own record for the dataset the ingest script
names (`scripts/ingest_ised_benchmarks.py`, CKAN dataset
`3f9e1080-4a08-4c0f-ace7-1b94a1afd61d`).

No Open Government Licence data file is distributed with this repository.
`scripts/ingest_ised_benchmarks.py` downloads the release when it is run, and
transforms it into `config/ised_benchmarks.json`, which is git-ignored.
That generated file and every report built from it carry the attribution the
licence requires:

  "Contains information licensed under the Open Government Licence – Canada.
   Source: ISED/StatCan Financial Performance Data."

The two benchmark files that *are* committed —
`tests/fixtures/ised_benchmarks_sample.json` and
`tests/fixtures/ised_benchmarks_cohorts_sample.json` — contain no FPD data.
Both are written by `scripts/gen_fixtures.py`, both have the same JSON shape as
the generated table, and every figure in them is invented. They carry no
attribution, because there is nothing in them to attribute.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Web fonts — none
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
No font file is distributed with this repository and none is fetched. The app
renders in the system font stack, so a browser loading it makes no third-party
request at all, and the Content-Security-Policy in `server/app.py` allows no
external font or stylesheet origin.


